IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part IX: Consequential and Related Amendments (ss 168-189) and
-- Coming into Force (s 190). Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here
-- is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT IS ENCODED. Ss 168 to 189 show only the placeholders [Amendments]: they amend other Acts and the text does not
-- reproduce the amendments, so there is nothing to encode (NOTES.md, coverage table, `inert`).
-- Section 190 fixes the days on which the Act as enacted came into force. These are the dates a rule-effective-date
-- check needs, so they are carried here as values with their @ref, and the lists of provisions that come into force
-- later than the rest are carried as lists, so that a question "was this provision in force on this day?" is
-- answered from the text.
--
-- The enactment (assent) date is not in this text: the title block gives only the citation S.C. 1996, c. 23.
--
-- A PROVISION is named by a STRING in the words of s 190 ("section 4", "subsection 5(6)", "paragraph 90(1)(d)").
-- That is a convention of this module, not of the Act: the list in s 190(2) and (3) is of provisions of the Act as
-- it was enacted, and a provision added later (Part VIII.4, for example) has its own commencement, which is not in
-- this text.

§ `Section 190(1) - the Act comes into force on June 30, 1996`

-- src:3171 | 190 (1) Except as otherwise provided in this section, this Act comes into force on June 30, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(1) (src:3171)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force` MEANS YearMonthDay 1996 6 30

§ `Section 190(2) - provisions in force on January 1, 1997`

-- src:3173 | (2) Section 4, subsection 5(6), sections 66 and 67, subsections 82(1) and (2), paragraphs 90(1)(d), (h) and (i), section 95 and subsections 96(4) and (5) come into force on January 1, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(2) (src:3173)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 190(2) the day on which the provisions listed in subsection (2) come into force` MEANS YearMonthDay 1997 1 1

-- src:3173 | (2) Section 4, subsection 5(6), sections 66 and 67, subsections 82(1) and (2), paragraphs 90(1)(d), (h) and (i), section 95 and subsections 96(4) and (5) come into force on January 1, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(2) (src:3173)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 190(2) the provisions listed in subsection (2)` MEANS
    LIST "section 4", "subsection 5(6)", "section 66", "section 67", "subsection 82(1)", "subsection 82(2)",
         "paragraph 90(1)(d)", "paragraph 90(1)(h)", "paragraph 90(1)(i)", "section 95",
         "subsection 96(4)", "subsection 96(5)"

