§ `Section 190(3.1) and (3.2) - two provisions in force on January 5, 1997, with a look-back`

-- Subsections 7.1(1) to (3) come into force on January 5, 1997, as (3.1) says; the Commission may nevertheless
-- take into account notices issued under 7.1(4) on or after June 30, 1996. A notice issued before that day may not be.
-- src:3191 | (3.1) Subsections 7.1(1) to (3) come into force on January 5, 1997, but in applying them the Commission may take into account notices issued under subsection 7.1(4) on or after June 30, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(3.1) (src:3191)
GIVEN `the day on which the notice under subsection 7.1(4) was issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 190(3.1) the Commission may take the notice into account in applying subsections 7.1(1) to (3)` MEANS
    `the day on which the notice under subsection 7.1(4) was issued` AT LEAST `s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force`

-- Subsection 19(3) comes into force on January 5, 1997; on and after that day the Commission may make deductions
-- under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i) for a failure to declare earnings for a period beginning on or after June 30, 1996.
-- (Section 159(1.1), in ei6-part-9-transitional, says "beginning after June 30, 1996": the two differ on June 30, 1996 itself.)
-- src:3193 | (3.2) Subsection 19(3) comes into force on January 5, 1997, but the Commission may make deductions under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i) on and after that date in respect of any failure to declare earnings for a period beginning on or after June 30, 1996.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(3.2) (src:3193)
GIVEN `the day of the deduction` IS A DATE
      `the first day of the period for which earnings were not declared` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 190(3.2) the Commission may make a deduction under subparagraph 19(3)(a)(i)` MEANS
        `the day of the deduction` AT LEAST `s 190(3) the day on which the provisions listed in subsection (3) come into force`
    AND `the first day of the period for which earnings were not declared` AT LEAST `s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force`

§ `Section 190(4) and (5) - Schedule II applies in the interim`

-- Schedule II applies in place of the provisions listed in subsections (2) and (3) from June 30, 1996 until those
-- provisions come into force. "Until the coming into force" is read as: on every day before the day the provision
-- comes into force (assumed, not ruled: fork F-ei6-5 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3171 | 190 (1) Except as otherwise provided in this section, this Act comes into force on June 30, 1996.
-- src:3173 | (2) Section 4, subsection 5(6), sections 66 and 67, subsections 82(1) and (2), paragraphs 90(1)(d), (h) and (i), section 95 and subsections 96(4) and (5) come into force on January 1, 1997.
-- src:3175 | (3) The following provisions come into force on January 5, 1997:
-- src:3176 | (a) the definitions major attachment claimant and minor attachment claimant in subsection 6(1);
-- src:3177 | (b) section 7;
-- src:3178 | (c) subsection 12(2);
-- src:3179 | (d) sections 14 to 17;
-- src:3180 | (e) subsection 19(2);
-- src:3181 | (f) subsection 28(4);
-- src:3182 | (g) paragraph 30(1)(a) and subsections 30(5) and (6);
-- src:3183 | (h) paragraph 31(c);
-- src:3184 | (i) paragraph 32(2)(c);
-- src:3185 | (j) subsection 38(3);
-- src:3186 | (k) section 55;
-- src:3187 | (l) paragraph 108(1)(h);
-- src:3188 | (l.1) subsection 153.1(3); and
-- src:3189 | (m) Schedule I.
-- src:3199 | (6) Sections 172 to 175 come into force on January 1, 1998.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(1), (2), (3), (6) (src:3171) (src:3173) (src:3175-3189) (src:3199)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `s 190 the day on which the provision comes into force` IS
    BRANCH IF elem provision (`s 190(2) the provisions listed in subsection (2)`) THEN `s 190(2) the day on which the provisions listed in subsection (2) come into force`
           IF elem provision (`s 190(3) the provisions listed in subsection (3)`) THEN `s 190(3) the day on which the provisions listed in subsection (3) come into force`
           IF elem provision (`s 190(6) the provisions listed in subsection (6)`) THEN `s 190(6) the day on which sections 172 to 175 come into force`
           OTHERWISE `s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force`

-- src:3195 | (4) The provisions set out in Schedule II apply in place of the provisions listed in subsections (2) and (3) from June 30, 1996 until the coming into force of those provisions.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(4) (src:3195)
GIVEN provision IS A STRING
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 190(4) Schedule II applies in place of the provision on the day` MEANS
        (elem provision (`s 190(2) the provisions listed in subsection (2)`) OR elem provision (`s 190(3) the provisions listed in subsection (3)`))
    AND day AT LEAST `s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force`
    AND day LESS THAN `s 190 the day on which the provision comes into force` provision

-- Paragraph 6 of Schedule II (the rate of weekly benefits) also continues, for a claimant whose benefit period began
-- on or after June 30, 1996 and before January 5, 1997, in place of sections 14, 16 and 17 for as long as that
-- benefit period runs.
-- src:3197 | (5) The provisions enacted by section 6 of Schedule II continue to apply in place of sections 14, 16 and 17 of this Act to claimants whose benefit periods begin on or after June 30, 1996 and before January 5, 1997.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(5) (src:3197)
GIVEN `the first day of the benefit period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 190(5) paragraph 6 of Schedule II continues to apply in place of sections 14, 16 and 17` MEANS
        `the first day of the benefit period` AT LEAST `s 190(1) the day this Act comes into force`
    AND `the first day of the benefit period` LESS THAN `s 190(3) the day on which the provisions listed in subsection (3) come into force`

§ `Section 190(6) - sections 172 to 175 in force on January 1, 1998`

-- src:3199 | (6) Sections 172 to 175 come into force on January 1, 1998.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(6) (src:3199)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 190(6) the day on which sections 172 to 175 come into force` MEANS YearMonthDay 1998 1 1

-- src:3199 | (6) Sections 172 to 175 come into force on January 1, 1998.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 190(6) (src:3199)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 190(6) the provisions listed in subsection (6)` MEANS LIST "section 172", "section 173", "section 174", "section 175"
